# The Dockerfile only COPYs pyproject.toml, uv.lock and app/, so nothing below
# could reach the image anyway. This is about the BUILD CONTEXT: everything in
# this directory is tar'd and sent to the Docker daemon before the build starts,
# whether the Dockerfile uses it or not. .venv alone is ~17 MB of pointless
# transfer on every build.
#
# It is also a safety net. The day someone writes `COPY . .`, this file is what
# stops a local virtualenv, the git history, and any stray .env from being
# baked into a published image.
#
# Added 2026-09-09 (D-14). gateway/.dockerignore is the same file.

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
tests/
README.md
.env
*.log
